  "preamble": "Debuccalization of the voiced alveolar fricative [z] to the glottal fricative [h] removes the oral constriction and the voicing, leaving only glottal friction. It characterizes Tahaggart (Tamahaq), the Tuareg of the Ahaggar, where Proto-Berber *z regularly appears as h; the dialect names reflect the split, Tamahaq against Tamasheq with š and Tamajaq with z or ž.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Debuccalization, Devoicing",
  "languageExamples": [
    {
      "language": "Tahaggart (Tamahaq)",
      "languageFamily": "Tuareg",
      "examples": [
